<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Aulerci Diablintes</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.) · capital Noviodunum Diablintum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Branch of the Aulerci in the western Mayenne whose Roman town at Jublains preserves one of the best surviving Roman forts in France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulerci">Aulerci</a> were a group of related peoples in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>; the Diablintes held the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jublains">Jublains</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayenne">Mayenne</a>, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aulerci-cenomani">Cenomani</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/redones">Redones</a>. Caesar names them among the allies of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veneti">Veneti</a>, and Ptolemy gives their town as Noviodunum.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Very little is known of their society before the conquest. They shared in the Atlantic and Armorican trade networks and struck coins of Armorican type.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After joining the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/veneti">Veneti</a> in 56 BCE they were defeated and absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-lugdunensis">Gallia Lugdunensis</a>. Their Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jublains">Noviodunum Diablintum</a> at Jublains, with its temple, baths, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and fortified store-building, declined in late antiquity when the civitas merged with that of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aulerci-cenomani">Cenomani</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/aulerci-diablintes.jpg" alt="Aulerci Diablintes" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Diablintes (peuple celtique de Gaule). Autorité émettrice de monnaie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Argent,_fonds_celtique,_Diablintes_-_btv1b11288748k_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Noviodunum Diablintum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Diablintes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=aulerci-diablintes" aria-label="Aulerci Diablintes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4750 530 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Aulerci Diablintes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5070 786h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5070 786h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=aulerci-diablintes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

